<table>
  <tr><th>Pad</th><th>Action</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">VOICE 0&ndash;5 (tap)</td><td class="act-name">Select Voice Page</td><td>Selects which voice&rsquo;s settings page is displayed. Active voice button lights in white. Voice buttons continue to flash in sync with playback (inverted: turning off briefly instead of turning white when a note plays).</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">Hold VOICE 0&ndash;5</td><td class="act-name">Voice Menu</td><td>Hold a voice pad (or tap a step while holding) to enter the Voice Menu and reassign its MIDI note on the 4&times;4 drum rack grid. Release to return.</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">STEP 1 (Row 1)</td><td class="act-name">Toggle Voice Protect</td><td>Protects the voice from all global actions (<code>ALL</code> and <code>FN1 + ALL</code> transforms, kits, and length changes). Its pattern stays untouched unless edited directly.</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">STEP 5 (Row 2)</td><td class="act-name">Ping-Pong Path</td><td>Forward-then-reverse bounce without repeating ends (e.g. <code>0 &rarr; 1 &rarr; 2 &rarr; 3 &rarr; 2 &rarr; 1</code>). Lights green when active, red when inactive.</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">STEP 6 (Row 2)</td><td class="act-name">Spiral Path</td><td>Outside-in clockwise grid traversal (<code>0, 1, 2, 3, 7, 11, 15, 14, 13, 12, 8, 4, 5, 6, 10, 9</code>). Lights green when active, red when inactive.</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">STEP 7 (Row 2)</td><td class="act-name">Phase Slip Path</td><td>Rotational phase slip (+1 step offset each completed cycle, staggered by +2 steps per voice). Lights green when active, red when inactive.</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">STEP 8 (Row 2)</td><td class="act-name">Mutate Path</td><td>Randomly switches between all unused path modifiers every 4 bars (Stutter, Weave, Drunken, Beat Ping-Pong, Broken Thirds, Downbeat Lock, Pair Swap, Turnaround, Pedal). Lights green when active, red when inactive.</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">MENU</td><td class="act-name">Exit Menu</td><td>Exits Menu Mode and returns to the sequencer.</td></tr>
</table>
