<section class="screen-page" id="page-voice-menu">
<h2 class="screen-title">Menu Mode: Voice Menu (MIDI Note Assignment)</h2>
<p class="note">
  Holding any <code>VOICE</code> pad for &ge;&thinsp;200ms in Menu Mode (or holding a voice pad and tapping a step pad)
  enters Voice Menu Mode. The 4&times;4 step grid mirrors the 16-pad Ableton Drum Rack (notes 36&ndash;51, bottom row 36&ndash;39 to top row 48&ndash;51).
  The currently assigned pad for the active voice illuminates in white (<code>COLOR_PPOS</code>). Pads assigned to other
  voices illuminate in their respective voice colors. Available / unassigned pads are dark.
  Tap any step pad (1&ndash;16) to reassign or swap notes. Tap another voice pad to switch the voice being edited.
  Release the held voice pad to return to Menu Mode, or tap <code>MENU</code> to exit directly back to the sequencer.
</p>

